              {
                "id": "R1-digest-ignores-mode",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "engine/skills/approval_digest.go:46-60",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The digest covers only each regular file's path and bytes. A permission change, such as adding the executable bit to an approved script, leaves the approval valid. The doc comment states this scope deliberately, and no concrete exploit is shown, so this is only a coverage gap.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/approval_digest.go:46-60",
                  "engine/skills/approval_digest.go:35-40"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              },
              {
                "id": "R1-walk-toctou",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "engine/skills/skillsfs/approvals.go:54-60",
                "severity": "WARNING",
                "claim": "The entry type comes from the directory listing, and the file is then opened with os.ReadFile. If an entry is swapped for a symlink or a FIFO between those two steps, the read could follow the link or block. This needs a concurrent local writer to the skill directory, so the impact is narrow.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "engine/skills/skillsfs/approvals.go:54-60"
                ],
                "evidence_class": "inferential",
                "causal_disposition": "introduced"
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "The change strengthens approval. It now digests every file of the skill instead of SKILL.md alone, removes the baseline exemption, and treats version-1 records as stale.",
              "Symlinks, pipes, sockets and devices are reported without being followed or opened, and they make the skill unverifiable (engine/skills/approval_digest.go, engine/skills/skillsfs/approvals.go).",
              "A symlinked skill directory is rejected, and unreadable files cause an error rather than being left out of the digest.",
              "The FIFO test confirms that reading the skill tree does not block on a named pipe.",
              "The lint baseline list that remains in engine/skills/approval_write.go is not an approval exemption.",
              "No reachable blocker-level exploit was found."
            ]
          }
        }
