            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Failure handling is fail-closed. An unreadable file, a non-directory or symlinked skill directory, or a walk error returns a non-ErrNotExist error. CheckApprovals turns that into APPROVAL_UNVERIFIABLE instead of leaving the file out of the digest (engine/skills/skillsfs/approvals.go, engine/skills/approval_gate.go).",
              "Hang risk is handled. ReadSkillTree only opens regular files and never opens FIFOs, sockets or devices. engine/skills/skillsfs/approvals_fifo_test.go covers the FIFO case with a 5-second timeout.",
              "Directory symlinks are not followed, because WalkDir reports them as non-directory entries. The root link check uses Lstat, so the walk cannot escape the skill directory.",
              "The record file's bytes are deliberately not read in the tree walk. A record that cannot be read is therefore reported by ReadRecord as unreadable, not as a skill that cannot be read.",
              "Removing the grandfathered baseline means v1 records and baseline skills with no record now report stale or missing. The change itself describes this as intended, and it fails closed, so it is not a resilience regression.",
              "Every file of each global skill is now read fully into memory on validate. No measured impact or realistic large-file case is shown in the candidate, so this is speculative and not reported."
            ]
          }
        }
